To: pkgsrc-security@NetBSD.org
Subject: pkg-vulnerabilities: two entries that can be narrowed (ncurses, libxml2)

Two sets of entries in pkg-vulnerabilities (rev 1.775) are written as
"every version", but the versions in question are fixed.  They make
pkg_admin audit report six issues on an up to date system.

1. ncurses, CVE-2025-69720

  ncurses-[0-9]*	buffer-overflow	https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-69720

  This is the stack buffer overflow in analyze_string() in
  progs/infocmp.c.  Upstream fixed it in the ncurses 6.5 20251213 patch,
  and ncurses 6.6 was released on 2025-12-30, so the release carries the
  fix.  In the 6.6 tarball, progs/infocmp.c is rev 1.177 (2025-12-27)
  and analyze_string() now clamps the length:

	if ((len = strlen(cp)) > MAX_TERMINFO_LENGTH)
	    len = MAX_TERMINFO_LENGTH;

  along with (len < sizeof(buf3)) guards on the CSI parameter paths.

  devel/ncurses in pkgsrc is at 6.6, so the entry could read

	ncurses<6.6	buffer-overflow	https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-69720

2. libxml2, five entries

  libxml2-[0-9]*	denial-of-service	https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2025-8732
  libxml2-[0-9]*	denial-of-service	https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-0989
  libxml2-[0-9]*	denial-of-service	https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-0990
  libxml2-[0-9]*	denial-of-service	https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-0992
  libxml2-[0-9]*	denial-of-service	https://nvd.nist.gov/vuln/detail/CVE-2026-1757

  All five are named as fixed in the libxml2 2.15.2 NEWS (2026-03-03);
  CVE-2025-8732 appears there as "catalog: fix stack overflow from
  self-referencing SGML CATALOG entries".  So these can become

	libxml2<2.15.2	...

  textproc/libxml2 in pkgsrc is still at 2.15.1; I have sent an update to
  2.15.3 to pkgsrc-users@ separately.

  The sixth entry for this package, CVE-2025-12863, is not named in the
  2.15.2 or 2.15.3 NEWS and I could not determine whether it is fixed, so
  I am not asking for that one to be changed.

  (As background for the "every version" entries: upstream declared
  libxml2 unmaintained in September 2025 and the GitLab page still says
  so, but releases resumed -- 2.15.2 and 2.15.3 were made by a different
  set of contributors.)

Thanks,

--
